{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WN7jzgNwUPAtWz6SaxRbZL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment data for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier definition. Each prediction needs a result_rationale explaining why that result would occur under median conditions.\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment and create predictions consistent with the median tier definition.\n\nMedian tier key characteristics:\n- CWM shows some degradation on repo-level but not catastrophic (unparseable 5-14%)\n- Classification has small but not clearly significant repo-level advantage\n- Re-repair experiment shows directional but non-significant improvement\n- Function-level null result replicates cleanly across seeds\n\n\n- Block correlation is partially confirmed with smaller effect sizes than initially simulated\n\nNow I'm looking at the specific metric ranges I need to work within for the predictions, including the function-level classification versus CWM F1 differences, multi-seed variability, repo-level performance bands for both approaches, and the unparseable rate for CWM.\n\nThe existing results show that function-level CLS and CWM are essentially equivalent—both hovering around 87% for pass and fail F1 scores—so the null hypothesis is already supported. Now I'm generating predictions for each planned experiment, starting with the multi-seed core approach. Now I'm working through the detailed predictions for each of these experimental approaches.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10554,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10554},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_