{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WN7jzgNwUPAtWz6SaxRbZL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Median档下论文核心叙事：function-level null result跨seed稳健复现，classification与CWM在简单任务上统计不可分；\n  repo-level出现方向性优势（2-5pp）但置信区间宽，CWM在repo-level暴露5-14%不可解析/截断率；\n  diagnostic re-repair呈方向性改善但未达显著性阈值。论文重心转向Claim 1（efficiency-equivalent + complexity-dependent advantage假说）\n  和Claim 3（oracle frontier characterization）的组合贡献，Claim 2降格为\"motivated hypothesis with directional evidence\"。\n  目标EMNLP Findings，Main需要强rebuttal prep。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: \"Classification和CWM各跑seeds {0, 1, 42}，报告mean±std F1，paired bootstrap CI\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_pass_f1_mean: 87.0\n      cls_pass_f1_std: 0.45\n      cls_fail_f1_mean: 87.8\n      cls_fail_f1_std: 0.52\n      cwm_pass_f1_mean: 87.2\n      cwm_pass_f1_std: 0.61\n      cwm_fail_f1_mean: 87.6\n      cwm_fail_f1_std: 0.58\n      mean_f1_diff_cls_minus_cwm: -0.1\n      paired_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.9, 0.7]\n      p_value_paired_test: 0.72\n      significant_at_005: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Seed 42的已有结果（CLS 87.1/87.9 vs CWM 87.31/87.71）已示null result。\n      Median档下function-level diff在[-0.5, 0.5]pp范围，multi-seed std在0.3-1.0。\n      4B LoRA在HumanEval/MBPP这类简单function-level数据上variance主要来自LoRA初始化和数据shuffle顺序，\n      因为task本身较简单（短执行输出，binary label明确），不同seed间波动有限但非零。\n      CWM的std略高于CLS因为generation任务对初始化更敏感（需要学习exact string matching而非binary boundary）。\n      Bootstrap CI跨零说明无法拒绝H0，正式确认function-level null result。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Function-Level Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Seed\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Overall Acc\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS\", \"0\", \"86.5\", \"87.3\", \"86.9\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"1\", \"87.4\", \"88.2\", \"87.8\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"42\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"Mean±Std\", \"87.0±0.45\", \"87.8±0.52\", \"87.4±0.46\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"0\", \"87.8\", \"88.1\", \"87.9\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"1\", \"86.6\", \"87.0\", \"86.8\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"42\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"Mean±Std\", \"87.2±0.61\", \"87.6±0.58\", \"87.4±0.56\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"paired bootstrap差值分布直方图，95%CI跨零，标注p=0.72\"\n    analysis: >\n      Null result跨三个seed稳健复现。两种formulation在function-level统计不可分（p=0.72），\n      CI覆盖零。这确认function-level task的简单性使得classification和generation等价——\n      短执行输出不触发CWM failure modes。该结果为complexity-dependent advantage叙事提供必要的baseline锚点。\n      CWM略高std符合预期：generation target空间更大，对随机初始化更敏感。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: \"单模型先生成~50 token执行推理trace再输出pass/fail，测试显式推理是否有帮助\"\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 87.5\n      ttj_fail_f1: 88.1\n      ttj_overall_acc: 87.8\n      ttj_vs_direct_cls_f1_diff: 0.15\n      ttj_unparseable_pct: 1.2\n      ttj_avg_output_tokens: 58\n      ttj_training_loss: 0.271\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下trace-then-judge与direct CLS的diff在[-2, 2]pp范围。在function-level上，\n      pass/fail判断所需的\"推理\"本质上很浅——输入代码通常<50行，test assertion直接明了。\n      额外的reasoning trace更多是\"复述\"而非\"深度推理\"，对4B模型而言增加了学习负担但也提供了\n      中间监督信号，两个效应大致抵消。结果略微正向（+0.15pp）但远不显著，说明在simple tasks上\n      显式推理既不帮助也不伤害。1.2%的unparseable来自偶尔的trace过长导致pass/fail token被截断。\n      该结果支持论文论点：classification的优势不是来自\"跳过推理\"而是来自\"避免output complexity\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Unparseable%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Direct CLS\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\", \"87.4\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"Trace-then-Judge\", \"87.5\", \"88.1\", \"87.8\", \"1.2\"]\n          - [\"CWM (generation)\", \"87.2\", \"87.6\", \"87.4\", \"0.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三种formulation（direct CLS / trace-then-judge / CWM）的F1 bar chart with error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace-then-judge与direct CLS差异微乎其微（+0.15pp），且低于multi-seed variance。\n      这排除了\"classification优势来自跳过执行推理\"的反驳——即使显式添加reasoning trace也不改变结果。\n      真正的区分因素是output format complexity（binary vs full string），不是reasoning depth。\n      1.2% unparseable率虽小但预示了repo-level上chain-of-thought+判断管线可能面临的格式问题。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-4B LoRA训练trajectory-level resolved/unresolved预测，隔离granularity效应\"\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 83.2\n      traj_resolved_f1: 82.8\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 83.5\n      traj_vs_pertest_cls_acc_gap: 4.2\n      instances_evaluated: 1890\n      training_loss: 0.312\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level任务将所有test concatenate成单个输入，要求模型判断\"整体是否resolved\"。\n      这比per-test classification更难：(1) 输入更长（多个test拼接），注意力被稀释；\n      (2) resolved需要ALL tests pass，unresolved只需ANY test fail——正负类的判断逻辑不对称；\n      (3) 数据量不变但每个problem_id只产生1个训练样本（vs per-test产生T个），有效训练集缩小。\n      Median档下4.2pp的gap合理——trajectory-level不是catastrophically差但明显弱于per-test。\n      这为Claim 2的granularity论点提供function-level证据（per-test > trajectory），\n      但因为这是function-level数据，gap主要来自信息论优势而非complexity advantage。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Granularity Comparison (Function-Level)\"\n        columns: [\"Granularity\", \"Accuracy\", \"Positive F1\", \"Negative F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Per-test CLS\", \"87.4\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\"]\n          - [\"Trajectory-level\", \"83.2\", \"82.8\", \"83.5\"]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+4.2\", \"+4.2\", \"+4.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-test vs trajectory-level accuracy随instance test数量T的变化曲线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test classification比trajectory-level高4.2pp，确认粒度细化本身有价值。\n      但需注意这个gap部分来自有效训练样本量差异（per-test产生~6x更多样本），\n      不完全是granularity的信息论优势。论文需要honest reporting这一confound。\n      该结果为diagnostic signal叙事提供support——per-test predictions的精度高于trajectory-level。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B→8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: \"CLS和CWM各从4B扩展到8B，测试classification advantage是否跨scale成立\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.2\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.0\n      cls_8b_acc: 89.6\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.0\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_acc: 89.4\n      cls_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.2\n      cwm_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.0\n      cls_vs_cwm_8b_diff: 0.2\n      cwm_8b_unparseable: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下function-level的CLS vs CWM diff在[-0.5, 0.5]。8B模型在function-level上\n      两种formulation都有~2pp提升（更大模型更好地理解code semantics），但diff依然近零（0.2pp）。\n      这是因为function-level的execution output足够短（<50 tokens），8B CWM有更多capacity\n      来精确匹配输出字符串。Null result在8B上持续成立，进一步支持\"advantage is complexity-dependent\n      not scale-dependent\"。CWM 8B unparseable仍为0因为function-level输出格式简单。\n      这个结果关键在于排除\"classification只在小模型上好\"的反驳。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Model Scale Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Δ vs CLS\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS\", \"4B\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\", \"87.4\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"4B\", \"87.2\", \"87.6\", \"87.4\", \"-0.0\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"8B\", \"89.2\", \"90.0\", \"89.6\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"8B\", \"89.0\", \"89.8\", \"89.4\", \"-0.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4B/8B x CLS/CWM的2x2 F1 line plot，可视化scaling behavior\"\n    analysis: >\n      两种formulation在function-level上scale equally well（~2pp gain from 4B→8B），\n      diff在8B时仍不显著。结合repo-level实验的预期结果（CLS优势出现），\n      可构建\"advantage threshold depends on output complexity not model scale\"的论点。\n      8B结果也提供了Pareto frontier的additional data points。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"对200个instance比较有/无per-test failure信息的repair resolve rate\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 31.5\n      with_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 33.0\n      resolve_rate_gain_pp: 1.5\n      n_instances: 200\n      p_value_mcnemar: 0.18\n      significant_at_005: false\n      instances_where_diagnostic_helped: 12\n      instances_where_diagnostic_hurt: 9\n      net_helped: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下re-repair gain在[0.5, 3]pp，方向正确但不显著。原因：\n      (1) Per-test predictions本身有~13%错误率，错误的diagnostic signal可能误导repair agent；\n      (2) 200 instances样本量下1.5pp差异的statistical power很低（需要~800+ instances达80% power）；\n      (3) function-level训练的verifier对repo-level数据的transfer有gap，\n      diagnostic signal质量比oracle scenario差很多；\n      (4) repair agent（SWE-agent类）本身的stochasticity也增加noise。\n      net_helped仅3个instance（12帮助-9伤害），说明diagnostic signal的precision不够高\n      导致部分case被误导。这支持将Claim 2降格为hypothesis。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Resolve Rate\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No diagnostic (baseline)\", \"31.5%\", \"[25.1, 38.3]\"]\n          - [\"With per-test diagnostic\", \"33.0%\", \"[26.5, 39.9]\"]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+1.5pp\", \"[-0.7, 3.7]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-instance paired comparison scatter plot: baseline vs diagnostic-aided resolve\"\n      - \"帮助/伤害/无影响的instance breakdown bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      方向性正向但p=0.18远不达显著。CI覆盖零。在median档下这是预期结果——\n      diagnostic signal exists但verifier精度不足以consistently改善downstream repair。\n      论文应honest报告为\"directional evidence suggesting per-test diagnostics may help\n      targeted re-repair, but our current verifier accuracy is insufficient for statistically\n      significant improvement\"。Claim 2降格为motivated hypothesis。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Precision-Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: \"在完整测试集上测量per-test failure prediction的precision/recall\"\n    expected_results:\n      fail_precision: 0.876\n      fail_recall: 0.882\n      pass_precision: 0.874\n      pass_recall: 0.868\n      macro_f1: 0.875\n      per_problem_fail_precision_std: 0.12\n      per_problem_fail_recall_std: 0.14\n      hard_subset_fail_f1: 0.78\n      easy_subset_fail_f1: 0.93\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些指标直接来自mvp-b-train已有结果（CLS model precision/recall）。\n      Median档的新增insight在于per-problem variance分析：fail prediction精度在problems间\n      差异较大（std~0.12-0.14），说明模型在某些problem types上远好于平均，在另一些上远差。\n      Hard subset（多步逻辑/复杂数据结构）的fail F1降至0.78，easy subset达0.93。\n      这种heterogeneity解释了为什么aggregate精度看似足够（87.6%），但downstream re-repair\n      效果不显著——恰好是hard cases最需要diagnostic signal，却也是prediction最不可靠的地方。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Per-Test Prediction Quality\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Overall\", \"Easy Subset\", \"Hard Subset\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Fail Precision\", \"0.876\", \"0.94\", \"0.79\"]\n          - [\"Fail Recall\", \"0.882\", \"0.92\", \"0.77\"]\n          - [\"Fail F1\", \"0.879\", \"0.93\", \"0.78\"]\n          - [\"Pass F1\", \"0.871\", \"0.93\", \"0.79\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-problem fail F1分布直方图，标注easy/hard分割\"\n      - \"precision-recall curve with operating points标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      Aggregate指标掩盖了problem-level heterogeneity。模型在easy cases上precision接近perfect\n      但在hard cases上降至~0.78。这为Claim 3（oracle frontier）提供empirical grounding：\n      per-test advantage在easy cases上不需要（trajectory-level已足够），在hard cases上\n      又受限于prediction quality。最优operating point取决于difficulty distribution。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P-Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: \"按F2P test数量分层的oracle per-test advantage分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_advantage: 0.020\n      T1_block_advantage: 0.109\n      T2_pct_instances: 16.5\n      T2_iid_advantage: 0.185\n      T2_block_advantage: 0.362\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 14.8\n      T3plus_iid_advantage: 0.241\n      T3plus_block_advantage: 0.384\n      weighted_avg_iid_advantage: 0.063\n      weighted_avg_block_advantage: 0.178\n    result_rationale: >\n      SWE-bench Verified的F2P分布高度右偏（68.7% T=1），T=1时per-test退化为trajectory-level\n      （只有一个test），advantage仅来自于该test的prediction精度差异（near zero under iid，\n      ~11pp under block correlation因为block结构在T=1时等价于instance-level bias）。\n      T=2时advantage跳增至~18.5pp(iid)/36.2pp(block)，因为两个独立test的joint correct\n      概率(0.85^2=0.72)远低于trajectory-level的single 0.85，per-test formulation通过\n      分别预测获得的信息增益开始明显。T=3+时advantage继续增长但边际递减。\n      关键insight：68.7%的instances是T=1，这解释了为什么overall weighted advantage在iid下\n      仅6.3pp——大部分instances上per-test没有structural advantage。\n      Block correlation将advantage从6.3pp放大到17.8pp，但这依赖于block假设的empirical validity。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Oracle Per-Test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count\", \"% Instances\", \"IID Adv@(70,85)\", \"Block Adv@(70,85)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", \"0.020\", \"0.109\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"16.5%\", \"0.185\", \"0.362\"]\n          - [\"T=3+\", \"14.8%\", \"0.241\", \"0.384\"]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", \"100%\", \"0.063\", \"0.178\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-test advantage vs T的折线图（iid和block两条线），x轴标注各T的instance占比\"\n      - \"SWE-bench Verified F2P count分布直方图\"\n    analysis: >\n      最强standalone finding之一。清晰展示per-test advantage集中在T≥2的31.3% instances。\n      这为practitioners提供决策框架：\"当你知道task有多个failing tests时deploy per-test verifier，\n      否则trajectory-level足够。\"Weighted average under iid仅6.3pp说明naive deployment\n      平均收益有限，但targeted deployment（只在T≥2上用）收益显著。\n      Block correlation的放大效应是论文的一个differentiated contribution——\n      但需要block-corr-empirical实验来validate假设强度。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: \"从训练好的模型predictions中测量actual error correlation structure\"\n    expected_results:\n      measured_intra_instance_corr: 0.18\n      simulated_block_corr_assumed: 0.30\n      iid_corr: 0.0\n      partial_block_fraction: 0.62\n      full_block_fraction: 0.15\n      iid_fraction: 0.23\n      effective_rho: 0.21\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下block correlation假设\"部分确认但effect size小于simulated\"。\n      Oracle simulation假设完全block correlation（ρ=1 within instance），但实际模型的\n      error correlation受多种因素调制：(1) 同一instance内不同tests测试不同功能时errors\n      较独立；(2) 但共享的code context理解错误导致correlated failures。\n      实测intra-instance correlation ~0.18，介于iid(0)和full-block(1)之间，\n      closer to iid than simulation assumed。这意味着oracle analysis中block curve\n      过于乐观——实际advantage介于iid和block曲线之间，但更接近iid端。\n      62% of instances show partial correlation, 15% show full block (all tests同时\n      对或同时错), 23% near iid。这部分支持block假设但削弱了它作为论文主要selling point的force。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Empirical Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [\"Correlation Model\", \"Assumed ρ\", \"Measured ρ\", \"Oracle Adv@(70,85)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"IID\", \"0.0\", \"—\", \"0.063\"]\n          - [\"Empirical\", \"—\", \"0.21\", \"~0.10\"]\n          - [\"Full Block\", \"1.0\", \"—\", \"0.178\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-instance error correlation heatmap（instances按T排序）\"\n      - \"oracle advantage vs correlation strength连续曲线，标注empirical operating point\"\n    analysis: >\n      Empirical correlation (ρ≈0.21) 介于iid和full-block之间。Oracle advantage的realistic\n      估计约10pp（在iid的6.3%和block的17.8%之间插值）。论文需要用empirical ρ重新计算\n      oracle curves而非only展示两个极端。这使Claim 3的贡献更nuanced但也更honest——\n      \"per-test advantage exists but is closer to the conservative iid estimate than\n      the optimistic block-correlated estimate.\"\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench PerTest Data Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker环境re-evaluation提取per-test labels，构建SWE-bench-PerTest数据集\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_evaluations: 438\n      docker_failures: 62\n      candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_samples: 7008\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 12.4\n      median_tests_per_instance: 6\n      f2p_tests_per_instance_mean: 3.0\n      p2p_tests_per_instance_mean: 9.4\n      regression_rate_p2p: 0.013\n      avg_code_length_tokens: 2800\n      avg_test_length_tokens: 450\n      construction_time_hours: 20\n    result_rationale: >\n      500 instances x 16 candidates中，Docker环境构建失败率约12.4%（62/500）——\n      SWE-bench Verified的Docker配置并非100%可复现，部分老repo依赖的package版本\n      在2026年已broken。成功的438 instances产生7008个(code, test_suite, candidate)组合。\n      每个instance平均12.4个tests（median 6，右偏），其中F2P平均3个、P2P平均9.4个。\n      P2P regression rate仅1.3%，与已完成的p2p-regression-rate实验一致（conclusion: negative），\n      说明P2P维度信息量有限。Code长度（~2800 tokens）远超function-level（<200 tokens），\n      这是repo-level experiments面临的核心挑战。构建耗时~20h with 16 parallel containers。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instances (successful)\", \"438\"]\n          - [\"Candidates per instance\", \"16\"]\n          - [\"Total (code, test) samples\", \"~54K\"]\n          - [\"Avg tests/instance\", \"12.4\"]\n          - [\"Avg F2P tests\", \"3.0\"]\n          - [\"Avg P2P tests\", \"9.4\"]\n          - [\"P2P regression rate\", \"1.3%\"]\n          - [\"Avg code tokens\", \"2800\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"test count per instance分布直方图（F2P / P2P分开）\"\n      - \"code length分布直方图，与function-level对比\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集构建成功但Docker失败率12.4%略高于预期。438个成功instances足够支撑repo-level实验。\n      P2P regression rate 1.3%确认了此前negative finding——P2P tests在当前benchmarks上\n      信息量极低。数据集本身是一个resource contribution，但需要注意438 instances中\n      68.7% T=1的F2P分布限制了per-test advantage的展示空间。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training and Evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"在SWE-bench-PerTest上fine-tune CLS和CWM，评估repo-level性能差异\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_4b_repo_pass_f1: 74.8\n      cls_4b_repo_fail_f1: 76.2\n      cls_4b_repo_acc: 75.5\n      cwm_4b_repo_pass_f1: 72.1\n      cwm_4b_repo_fail_f1: 73.8\n      cwm_4b_repo_acc: 73.0\n      repo_level_gap_pp: 2.5\n      cwm_repo_unparseable_pct: 8.7\n      cwm_repo_truncated_pct: 3.2\n      cwm_repo_unparseable_or_truncated_total: 11.9\n      cls_8b_repo_acc: 78.3\n      cwm_8b_repo_acc: 75.9\n      repo_level_gap_8b_pp: 2.4\n      training_instances: 350\n      eval_instances: 88\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档核心预测：repo-level CLS F1在[72,80]，CWM F1在[68,77]，gap在[2,5]pp。\n      CWM在repo-level暴露两大failure mode：(1) unparseable 8.7%——repo-level execution output\n      格式多样（tracebacks, assertion messages, log outputs），CWM生成的output经常与\n      ground truth在formatting上不匹配导致exact match失败；(2) truncated 3.2%——\n      部分test的execution output超过model max output tokens（4096），generation被截断。\n      CLS完全不受这两个问题影响因为输出固定为单token。\n      2.5pp的gap是\"modest advantage\"——方向一致且可解释（CWM failure modes documented），\n      但在88个eval instances上可能不显著（需要bootstrap CI）。\n      8B模型上gap持续（2.4pp），说明failure modes不是纯capacity问题而是formulation inherent。\n      这是论文能否claim \"complexity-dependent advantage\" 的关键实验——2.5pp的gap exist\n      但need careful statistical reporting。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Repo-Level Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Unparseable%\", \"Truncated%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS\", \"4B\", \"74.8\", \"76.2\", \"75.5\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"4B\", \"72.1\", \"73.8\", \"73.0\", \"8.7\", \"3.2\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"8B\", \"77.5\", \"79.1\", \"78.3\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"8B\", \"75.2\", \"76.7\", \"75.9\", \"5.8\", \"2.1\"]\n          - name: \"Table 12: Function-Level vs Repo-Level Gap\"\n            columns: [\"Level\", \"CLS Acc\", \"CWM Acc\", \"Gap\"]\n            rows:\n              - [\"Function\", \"87.4\", \"87.4\", \"0.0\"]\n              - [\"Repo\", \"75.5\", \"73.0\", \"2.5\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"function-level vs repo-level的CLS/CWM paired bar chart，可视化complexity-dependent gap\"\n      - \"CWM failure mode breakdown pie chart（correct / unparseable / truncated / wrong prediction）\"\n      - \"repo-level per-instance accuracy scatter: CLS vs CWM，标注CWM failure instances\"\n    analysis: >\n      Repo-level gap 2.5pp存在但modest。CWM failure modes（11.9% unparseable+truncated）\n      是gap的主要来源——如果exclude这些cases，剩余instances上CLS vs CWM差异进一步缩小。\n      这支持\"advantage comes from robustness to output complexity\"但effect size小于initial hopes。\n      论文需要carefully frame：不是\"classification远优于generation\"而是\"classification更robust，\n      advantage grows with complexity but the median SWE-bench instance doesn't push the threshold hard enough\n      for a large gap\"。配合efficiency argument（1 token vs N tokens）仍有compelling story。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Zero-Shot Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot作为trajectory-level和per-test judge baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_8b_traj_acc: 64.2\n      qwen_8b_pertest_acc: 61.8\n      qwen_32b_traj_acc: 71.5\n      qwen_32b_pertest_acc: 68.3\n      qwen_8b_pertest_unparseable: 4.8\n      qwen_32b_pertest_unparseable: 2.1\n      finetuned_4b_pertest_acc: 75.5\n      finetuned_advantage_vs_32b_zeroshot: 7.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM judges在repo-level上表现显著弱于fine-tuned小模型——\n      这是因为pass/fail prediction需要precise code semantic理解而非general reasoning。\n      32B zero-shot (71.5%) 仍低于fine-tuned 4B (75.5%)，证明task-specific fine-tuning\n      的价值。Per-test accuracy低于trajectory-level是因为per-test需要更fine-grained判断，\n      zero-shot模型在没有见过per-test format的情况下表现更差。\n      Unparseable rates（4.8%/2.1%）来自zero-shot output format不稳定。\n      这些baselines在Pareto frontier图中提供重要参考点：accuracy vs inference cost曲线上，\n      fine-tuned 4B CLS位于左上角（高accuracy, 低cost），32B zero-shot位于右下（中accuracy, 高cost）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: LLM-as-Judge Baselines (Repo-Level)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Mode\", \"Accuracy\", \"Unparseable%\", \"Cost (rel)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B ZS\", \"Traj\", \"64.2\", \"—\", \"1x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B ZS\", \"Per-test\", \"61.8\", \"4.8\", \"1x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B ZS\", \"Traj\", \"71.5\", \"—\", \"4x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B ZS\", \"Per-test\", \"68.3\", \"2.1\", \"4x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B FT\", \"Per-test CLS\", \"75.5\", \"0.0\", \"0.5x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier: accuracy vs inference cost，标注所有model configurations\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B dominates 32B zero-shot on both accuracy AND cost——\n      这是论文efficiency narrative的强支持。Pareto frontier清晰展示fine-tuned classification\n      是当前最优cost-accuracy tradeoff。但需注意zero-shot baselines没有经过prompt engineering\n      优化，sophisticated prompting可能缩小gap。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: \"K=3 majority voting for per-test classification\"\n    expected_results:\n      single_pass_f1: 87.0\n      majority_k3_pass_f1: 88.4\n      single_fail_f1: 87.8\n      majority_k3_fail_f1: 89.1\n      accuracy_gain_pp: 1.2\n      inference_cost_multiplier: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting (K=3)通过self-consistency提供小幅提升（~1.2pp）。\n      在function-level上，模型的prediction已经较confident（87%+ F1），\n      大部分predictions在3次run中一致——improvement来自边界case的tiebreaking。\n      1.2pp gain with 3x cost在Pareto frontier上可能不如直接用更大模型cost-effective。\n      这个实验主要是completeness——展示test-time compute scaling在per-test上可以工作但\n      边际收益递减快。对于median档论文可能放到appendix。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1: Majority Voting Results (Function-Level)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Cost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single (K=1)\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\", \"87.4\", \"1x\"]\n          - [\"Majority (K=3)\", \"88.4\", \"89.1\", \"88.7\", \"3x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"accuracy vs K curve (K=1,3,5), diminishing returns可视化\"\n    analysis: >\n      Majority voting提供modest gains，不足以改变论文main narrative。\n      可作为appendix展示test-time compute scaling dim，或在Pareto frontier中\n      提供additional data point。不建议作为main contribution。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10554,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10554},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e613193-8e9c-4068-baa4-713d93e186c0","uuid":"69e146e9-89cc-41b4-a684-811ca8044b63"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":215157,"duration_api_ms":216371,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Median档下论文核心叙事：function-level null result跨seed稳健复现，classification与CWM在简单任务上统计不可分；\n  repo-level出现方向性优势（2-5pp）但置信区间宽，CWM在repo-level暴露5-14%不可解析/截断率；\n  diagnostic re-repair呈方向性改善但未达显著性阈值。论文重心转向Claim 1（efficiency-equivalent + complexity-dependent advantage假说）\n  和Claim 3（oracle frontier characterization）的组合贡献，Claim 2降格为\"motivated hypothesis with directional evidence\"。\n  目标EMNLP Findings，Main需要强rebuttal prep。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: \"Classification和CWM各跑seeds {0, 1, 42}，报告mean±std F1，paired bootstrap CI\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_pass_f1_mean: 87.0\n      cls_pass_f1_std: 0.45\n      cls_fail_f1_mean: 87.8\n      cls_fail_f1_std: 0.52\n      cwm_pass_f1_mean: 87.2\n      cwm_pass_f1_std: 0.61\n      cwm_fail_f1_mean: 87.6\n      cwm_fail_f1_std: 0.58\n      mean_f1_diff_cls_minus_cwm: -0.1\n      paired_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.9, 0.7]\n      p_value_paired_test: 0.72\n      significant_at_005: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Seed 42的已有结果（CLS 87.1/87.9 vs CWM 87.31/87.71）已示null result。\n      Median档下function-level diff在[-0.5, 0.5]pp范围，multi-seed std在0.3-1.0。\n      4B LoRA在HumanEval/MBPP这类简单function-level数据上variance主要来自LoRA初始化和数据shuffle顺序，\n      因为task本身较简单（短执行输出，binary label明确），不同seed间波动有限但非零。\n      CWM的std略高于CLS因为generation任务对初始化更敏感（需要学习exact string matching而非binary boundary）。\n      Bootstrap CI跨零说明无法拒绝H0，正式确认function-level null result。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Function-Level Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Seed\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Overall Acc\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS\", \"0\", \"86.5\", \"87.3\", \"86.9\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"1\", \"87.4\", \"88.2\", \"87.8\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"42\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"Mean±Std\", \"87.0±0.45\", \"87.8±0.52\", \"87.4±0.46\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"0\", \"87.8\", \"88.1\", \"87.9\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"1\", \"86.6\", \"87.0\", \"86.8\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"42\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"Mean±Std\", \"87.2±0.61\", \"87.6±0.58\", \"87.4±0.56\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"paired bootstrap差值分布直方图，95%CI跨零，标注p=0.72\"\n    analysis: >\n      Null result跨三个seed稳健复现。两种formulation在function-level统计不可分（p=0.72），\n      CI覆盖零。这确认function-level task的简单性使得classification和generation等价——\n      短执行输出不触发CWM failure modes。该结果为complexity-dependent advantage叙事提供必要的baseline锚点。\n      CWM略高std符合预期：generation target空间更大，对随机初始化更敏感。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: \"单模型先生成~50 token执行推理trace再输出pass/fail，测试显式推理是否有帮助\"\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 87.5\n      ttj_fail_f1: 88.1\n      ttj_overall_acc: 87.8\n      ttj_vs_direct_cls_f1_diff: 0.15\n      ttj_unparseable_pct: 1.2\n      ttj_avg_output_tokens: 58\n      ttj_training_loss: 0.271\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下trace-then-judge与direct CLS的diff在[-2, 2]pp范围。在function-level上，\n      pass/fail判断所需的\"推理\"本质上很浅——输入代码通常<50行，test assertion直接明了。\n      额外的reasoning trace更多是\"复述\"而非\"深度推理\"，对4B模型而言增加了学习负担但也提供了\n      中间监督信号，两个效应大致抵消。结果略微正向（+0.15pp）但远不显著，说明在simple tasks上\n      显式推理既不帮助也不伤害。1.2%的unparseable来自偶尔的trace过长导致pass/fail token被截断。\n      该结果支持论文论点：classification的优势不是来自\"跳过推理\"而是来自\"避免output complexity\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Unparseable%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Direct CLS\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\", \"87.4\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"Trace-then-Judge\", \"87.5\", \"88.1\", \"87.8\", \"1.2\"]\n          - [\"CWM (generation)\", \"87.2\", \"87.6\", \"87.4\", \"0.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三种formulation（direct CLS / trace-then-judge / CWM）的F1 bar chart with error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace-then-judge与direct CLS差异微乎其微（+0.15pp），且低于multi-seed variance。\n      这排除了\"classification优势来自跳过执行推理\"的反驳——即使显式添加reasoning trace也不改变结果。\n      真正的区分因素是output format complexity（binary vs full string），不是reasoning depth。\n      1.2% unparseable率虽小但预示了repo-level上chain-of-thought+判断管线可能面临的格式问题。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-4B LoRA训练trajectory-level resolved/unresolved预测，隔离granularity效应\"\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 83.2\n      traj_resolved_f1: 82.8\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 83.5\n      traj_vs_pertest_cls_acc_gap: 4.2\n      instances_evaluated: 1890\n      training_loss: 0.312\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level任务将所有test concatenate成单个输入，要求模型判断\"整体是否resolved\"。\n      这比per-test classification更难：(1) 输入更长（多个test拼接），注意力被稀释；\n      (2) resolved需要ALL tests pass，unresolved只需ANY test fail——正负类的判断逻辑不对称；\n      (3) 数据量不变但每个problem_id只产生1个训练样本（vs per-test产生T个），有效训练集缩小。\n      Median档下4.2pp的gap合理——trajectory-level不是catastrophically差但明显弱于per-test。\n      这为Claim 2的granularity论点提供function-level证据（per-test > trajectory），\n      但因为这是function-level数据，gap主要来自信息论优势而非complexity advantage。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Granularity Comparison (Function-Level)\"\n        columns: [\"Granularity\", \"Accuracy\", \"Positive F1\", \"Negative F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Per-test CLS\", \"87.4\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\"]\n          - [\"Trajectory-level\", \"83.2\", \"82.8\", \"83.5\"]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+4.2\", \"+4.2\", \"+4.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-test vs trajectory-level accuracy随instance test数量T的变化曲线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test classification比trajectory-level高4.2pp，确认粒度细化本身有价值。\n      但需注意这个gap部分来自有效训练样本量差异（per-test产生~6x更多样本），\n      不完全是granularity的信息论优势。论文需要honest reporting这一confound。\n      该结果为diagnostic signal叙事提供support——per-test predictions的精度高于trajectory-level。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B→8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: \"CLS和CWM各从4B扩展到8B，测试classification advantage是否跨scale成立\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.2\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.0\n      cls_8b_acc: 89.6\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.0\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_acc: 89.4\n      cls_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.2\n      cwm_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.0\n      cls_vs_cwm_8b_diff: 0.2\n      cwm_8b_unparseable: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下function-level的CLS vs CWM diff在[-0.5, 0.5]。8B模型在function-level上\n      两种formulation都有~2pp提升（更大模型更好地理解code semantics），但diff依然近零（0.2pp）。\n      这是因为function-level的execution output足够短（<50 tokens），8B CWM有更多capacity\n      来精确匹配输出字符串。Null result在8B上持续成立，进一步支持\"advantage is complexity-dependent\n      not scale-dependent\"。CWM 8B unparseable仍为0因为function-level输出格式简单。\n      这个结果关键在于排除\"classification只在小模型上好\"的反驳。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Model Scale Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Δ vs CLS\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS\", \"4B\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\", \"87.4\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"4B\", \"87.2\", \"87.6\", \"87.4\", \"-0.0\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"8B\", \"89.2\", \"90.0\", \"89.6\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"8B\", \"89.0\", \"89.8\", \"89.4\", \"-0.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4B/8B x CLS/CWM的2x2 F1 line plot，可视化scaling behavior\"\n    analysis: >\n      两种formulation在function-level上scale equally well（~2pp gain from 4B→8B），\n      diff在8B时仍不显著。结合repo-level实验的预期结果（CLS优势出现），\n      可构建\"advantage threshold depends on output complexity not model scale\"的论点。\n      8B结果也提供了Pareto frontier的additional data points。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: \"对200个instance比较有/无per-test failure信息的repair resolve rate\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 31.5\n      with_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 33.0\n      resolve_rate_gain_pp: 1.5\n      n_instances: 200\n      p_value_mcnemar: 0.18\n      significant_at_005: false\n      instances_where_diagnostic_helped: 12\n      instances_where_diagnostic_hurt: 9\n      net_helped: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下re-repair gain在[0.5, 3]pp，方向正确但不显著。原因：\n      (1) Per-test predictions本身有~13%错误率，错误的diagnostic signal可能误导repair agent；\n      (2) 200 instances样本量下1.5pp差异的statistical power很低（需要~800+ instances达80% power）；\n      (3) function-level训练的verifier对repo-level数据的transfer有gap，\n      diagnostic signal质量比oracle scenario差很多；\n      (4) repair agent（SWE-agent类）本身的stochasticity也增加noise。\n      net_helped仅3个instance（12帮助-9伤害），说明diagnostic signal的precision不够高\n      导致部分case被误导。这支持将Claim 2降格为hypothesis。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Resolve Rate\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No diagnostic (baseline)\", \"31.5%\", \"[25.1, 38.3]\"]\n          - [\"With per-test diagnostic\", \"33.0%\", \"[26.5, 39.9]\"]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+1.5pp\", \"[-0.7, 3.7]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-instance paired comparison scatter plot: baseline vs diagnostic-aided resolve\"\n      - \"帮助/伤害/无影响的instance breakdown bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      方向性正向但p=0.18远不达显著。CI覆盖零。在median档下这是预期结果——\n      diagnostic signal exists但verifier精度不足以consistently改善downstream repair。\n      论文应honest报告为\"directional evidence suggesting per-test diagnostics may help\n      targeted re-repair, but our current verifier accuracy is insufficient for statistically\n      significant improvement\"。Claim 2降格为motivated hypothesis。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Precision-Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: \"在完整测试集上测量per-test failure prediction的precision/recall\"\n    expected_results:\n      fail_precision: 0.876\n      fail_recall: 0.882\n      pass_precision: 0.874\n      pass_recall: 0.868\n      macro_f1: 0.875\n      per_problem_fail_precision_std: 0.12\n      per_problem_fail_recall_std: 0.14\n      hard_subset_fail_f1: 0.78\n      easy_subset_fail_f1: 0.93\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些指标直接来自mvp-b-train已有结果（CLS model precision/recall）。\n      Median档的新增insight在于per-problem variance分析：fail prediction精度在problems间\n      差异较大（std~0.12-0.14），说明模型在某些problem types上远好于平均，在另一些上远差。\n      Hard subset（多步逻辑/复杂数据结构）的fail F1降至0.78，easy subset达0.93。\n      这种heterogeneity解释了为什么aggregate精度看似足够（87.6%），但downstream re-repair\n      效果不显著——恰好是hard cases最需要diagnostic signal，却也是prediction最不可靠的地方。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Per-Test Prediction Quality\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Overall\", \"Easy Subset\", \"Hard Subset\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Fail Precision\", \"0.876\", \"0.94\", \"0.79\"]\n          - [\"Fail Recall\", \"0.882\", \"0.92\", \"0.77\"]\n          - [\"Fail F1\", \"0.879\", \"0.93\", \"0.78\"]\n          - [\"Pass F1\", \"0.871\", \"0.93\", \"0.79\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-problem fail F1分布直方图，标注easy/hard分割\"\n      - \"precision-recall curve with operating points标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      Aggregate指标掩盖了problem-level heterogeneity。模型在easy cases上precision接近perfect\n      但在hard cases上降至~0.78。这为Claim 3（oracle frontier）提供empirical grounding：\n      per-test advantage在easy cases上不需要（trajectory-level已足够），在hard cases上\n      又受限于prediction quality。最优operating point取决于difficulty distribution。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P-Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: \"按F2P test数量分层的oracle per-test advantage分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_advantage: 0.020\n      T1_block_advantage: 0.109\n      T2_pct_instances: 16.5\n      T2_iid_advantage: 0.185\n      T2_block_advantage: 0.362\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 14.8\n      T3plus_iid_advantage: 0.241\n      T3plus_block_advantage: 0.384\n      weighted_avg_iid_advantage: 0.063\n      weighted_avg_block_advantage: 0.178\n    result_rationale: >\n      SWE-bench Verified的F2P分布高度右偏（68.7% T=1），T=1时per-test退化为trajectory-level\n      （只有一个test），advantage仅来自于该test的prediction精度差异（near zero under iid，\n      ~11pp under block correlation因为block结构在T=1时等价于instance-level bias）。\n      T=2时advantage跳增至~18.5pp(iid)/36.2pp(block)，因为两个独立test的joint correct\n      概率(0.85^2=0.72)远低于trajectory-level的single 0.85，per-test formulation通过\n      分别预测获得的信息增益开始明显。T=3+时advantage继续增长但边际递减。\n      关键insight：68.7%的instances是T=1，这解释了为什么overall weighted advantage在iid下\n      仅6.3pp——大部分instances上per-test没有structural advantage。\n      Block correlation将advantage从6.3pp放大到17.8pp，但这依赖于block假设的empirical validity。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Oracle Per-Test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count\", \"% Instances\", \"IID Adv@(70,85)\", \"Block Adv@(70,85)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", \"0.020\", \"0.109\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"16.5%\", \"0.185\", \"0.362\"]\n          - [\"T=3+\", \"14.8%\", \"0.241\", \"0.384\"]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", \"100%\", \"0.063\", \"0.178\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-test advantage vs T的折线图（iid和block两条线），x轴标注各T的instance占比\"\n      - \"SWE-bench Verified F2P count分布直方图\"\n    analysis: >\n      最强standalone finding之一。清晰展示per-test advantage集中在T≥2的31.3% instances。\n      这为practitioners提供决策框架：\"当你知道task有多个failing tests时deploy per-test verifier，\n      否则trajectory-level足够。\"Weighted average under iid仅6.3pp说明naive deployment\n      平均收益有限，但targeted deployment（只在T≥2上用）收益显著。\n      Block correlation的放大效应是论文的一个differentiated contribution——\n      但需要block-corr-empirical实验来validate假设强度。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: \"从训练好的模型predictions中测量actual error correlation structure\"\n    expected_results:\n      measured_intra_instance_corr: 0.18\n      simulated_block_corr_assumed: 0.30\n      iid_corr: 0.0\n      partial_block_fraction: 0.62\n      full_block_fraction: 0.15\n      iid_fraction: 0.23\n      effective_rho: 0.21\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下block correlation假设\"部分确认但effect size小于simulated\"。\n      Oracle simulation假设完全block correlation（ρ=1 within instance），但实际模型的\n      error correlation受多种因素调制：(1) 同一instance内不同tests测试不同功能时errors\n      较独立；(2) 但共享的code context理解错误导致correlated failures。\n      实测intra-instance correlation ~0.18，介于iid(0)和full-block(1)之间，\n      closer to iid than simulation assumed。这意味着oracle analysis中block curve\n      过于乐观——实际advantage介于iid和block曲线之间，但更接近iid端。\n      62% of instances show partial correlation, 15% show full block (all tests同时\n      对或同时错), 23% near iid。这部分支持block假设但削弱了它作为论文主要selling point的force。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Empirical Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [\"Correlation Model\", \"Assumed ρ\", \"Measured ρ\", \"Oracle Adv@(70,85)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"IID\", \"0.0\", \"—\", \"0.063\"]\n          - [\"Empirical\", \"—\", \"0.21\", \"~0.10\"]\n          - [\"Full Block\", \"1.0\", \"—\", \"0.178\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"per-instance error correlation heatmap（instances按T排序）\"\n      - \"oracle advantage vs correlation strength连续曲线，标注empirical operating point\"\n    analysis: >\n      Empirical correlation (ρ≈0.21) 介于iid和full-block之间。Oracle advantage的realistic\n      估计约10pp（在iid的6.3%和block的17.8%之间插值）。论文需要用empirical ρ重新计算\n      oracle curves而非only展示两个极端。这使Claim 3的贡献更nuanced但也更honest——\n      \"per-test advantage exists but is closer to the conservative iid estimate than\n      the optimistic block-correlated estimate.\"\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench PerTest Data Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: \"Docker环境re-evaluation提取per-test labels，构建SWE-bench-PerTest数据集\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_evaluations: 438\n      docker_failures: 62\n      candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_samples: 7008\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 12.4\n      median_tests_per_instance: 6\n      f2p_tests_per_instance_mean: 3.0\n      p2p_tests_per_instance_mean: 9.4\n      regression_rate_p2p: 0.013\n      avg_code_length_tokens: 2800\n      avg_test_length_tokens: 450\n      construction_time_hours: 20\n    result_rationale: >\n      500 instances x 16 candidates中，Docker环境构建失败率约12.4%（62/500）——\n      SWE-bench Verified的Docker配置并非100%可复现，部分老repo依赖的package版本\n      在2026年已broken。成功的438 instances产生7008个(code, test_suite, candidate)组合。\n      每个instance平均12.4个tests（median 6，右偏），其中F2P平均3个、P2P平均9.4个。\n      P2P regression rate仅1.3%，与已完成的p2p-regression-rate实验一致（conclusion: negative），\n      说明P2P维度信息量有限。Code长度（~2800 tokens）远超function-level（<200 tokens），\n      这是repo-level experiments面临的核心挑战。构建耗时~20h with 16 parallel containers。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instances (successful)\", \"438\"]\n          - [\"Candidates per instance\", \"16\"]\n          - [\"Total (code, test) samples\", \"~54K\"]\n          - [\"Avg tests/instance\", \"12.4\"]\n          - [\"Avg F2P tests\", \"3.0\"]\n          - [\"Avg P2P tests\", \"9.4\"]\n          - [\"P2P regression rate\", \"1.3%\"]\n          - [\"Avg code tokens\", \"2800\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"test count per instance分布直方图（F2P / P2P分开）\"\n      - \"code length分布直方图，与function-level对比\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集构建成功但Docker失败率12.4%略高于预期。438个成功instances足够支撑repo-level实验。\n      P2P regression rate 1.3%确认了此前negative finding——P2P tests在当前benchmarks上\n      信息量极低。数据集本身是一个resource contribution，但需要注意438 instances中\n      68.7% T=1的F2P分布限制了per-test advantage的展示空间。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training and Evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: \"在SWE-bench-PerTest上fine-tune CLS和CWM，评估repo-level性能差异\"\n    expected_results:\n      cls_4b_repo_pass_f1: 74.8\n      cls_4b_repo_fail_f1: 76.2\n      cls_4b_repo_acc: 75.5\n      cwm_4b_repo_pass_f1: 72.1\n      cwm_4b_repo_fail_f1: 73.8\n      cwm_4b_repo_acc: 73.0\n      repo_level_gap_pp: 2.5\n      cwm_repo_unparseable_pct: 8.7\n      cwm_repo_truncated_pct: 3.2\n      cwm_repo_unparseable_or_truncated_total: 11.9\n      cls_8b_repo_acc: 78.3\n      cwm_8b_repo_acc: 75.9\n      repo_level_gap_8b_pp: 2.4\n      training_instances: 350\n      eval_instances: 88\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档核心预测：repo-level CLS F1在[72,80]，CWM F1在[68,77]，gap在[2,5]pp。\n      CWM在repo-level暴露两大failure mode：(1) unparseable 8.7%——repo-level execution output\n      格式多样（tracebacks, assertion messages, log outputs），CWM生成的output经常与\n      ground truth在formatting上不匹配导致exact match失败；(2) truncated 3.2%——\n      部分test的execution output超过model max output tokens（4096），generation被截断。\n      CLS完全不受这两个问题影响因为输出固定为单token。\n      2.5pp的gap是\"modest advantage\"——方向一致且可解释（CWM failure modes documented），\n      但在88个eval instances上可能不显著（需要bootstrap CI）。\n      8B模型上gap持续（2.4pp），说明failure modes不是纯capacity问题而是formulation inherent。\n      这是论文能否claim \"complexity-dependent advantage\" 的关键实验——2.5pp的gap exist\n      但need careful statistical reporting。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Repo-Level Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Unparseable%\", \"Truncated%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CLS\", \"4B\", \"74.8\", \"76.2\", \"75.5\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"4B\", \"72.1\", \"73.8\", \"73.0\", \"8.7\", \"3.2\"]\n          - [\"CLS\", \"8B\", \"77.5\", \"79.1\", \"78.3\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"CWM\", \"8B\", \"75.2\", \"76.7\", \"75.9\", \"5.8\", \"2.1\"]\n          - name: \"Table 12: Function-Level vs Repo-Level Gap\"\n            columns: [\"Level\", \"CLS Acc\", \"CWM Acc\", \"Gap\"]\n            rows:\n              - [\"Function\", \"87.4\", \"87.4\", \"0.0\"]\n              - [\"Repo\", \"75.5\", \"73.0\", \"2.5\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"function-level vs repo-level的CLS/CWM paired bar chart，可视化complexity-dependent gap\"\n      - \"CWM failure mode breakdown pie chart（correct / unparseable / truncated / wrong prediction）\"\n      - \"repo-level per-instance accuracy scatter: CLS vs CWM，标注CWM failure instances\"\n    analysis: >\n      Repo-level gap 2.5pp存在但modest。CWM failure modes（11.9% unparseable+truncated）\n      是gap的主要来源——如果exclude这些cases，剩余instances上CLS vs CWM差异进一步缩小。\n      这支持\"advantage comes from robustness to output complexity\"但effect size小于initial hopes。\n      论文需要carefully frame：不是\"classification远优于generation\"而是\"classification更robust，\n      advantage grows with complexity but the median SWE-bench instance doesn't push the threshold hard enough\n      for a large gap\"。配合efficiency argument（1 token vs N tokens）仍有compelling story。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Zero-Shot Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot作为trajectory-level和per-test judge baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_8b_traj_acc: 64.2\n      qwen_8b_pertest_acc: 61.8\n      qwen_32b_traj_acc: 71.5\n      qwen_32b_pertest_acc: 68.3\n      qwen_8b_pertest_unparseable: 4.8\n      qwen_32b_pertest_unparseable: 2.1\n      finetuned_4b_pertest_acc: 75.5\n      finetuned_advantage_vs_32b_zeroshot: 7.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM judges在repo-level上表现显著弱于fine-tuned小模型——\n      这是因为pass/fail prediction需要precise code semantic理解而非general reasoning。\n      32B zero-shot (71.5%) 仍低于fine-tuned 4B (75.5%)，证明task-specific fine-tuning\n      的价值。Per-test accuracy低于trajectory-level是因为per-test需要更fine-grained判断，\n      zero-shot模型在没有见过per-test format的情况下表现更差。\n      Unparseable rates（4.8%/2.1%）来自zero-shot output format不稳定。\n      这些baselines在Pareto frontier图中提供重要参考点：accuracy vs inference cost曲线上，\n      fine-tuned 4B CLS位于左上角（高accuracy, 低cost），32B zero-shot位于右下（中accuracy, 高cost）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: LLM-as-Judge Baselines (Repo-Level)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Mode\", \"Accuracy\", \"Unparseable%\", \"Cost (rel)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B ZS\", \"Traj\", \"64.2\", \"—\", \"1x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B ZS\", \"Per-test\", \"61.8\", \"4.8\", \"1x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B ZS\", \"Traj\", \"71.5\", \"—\", \"4x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B ZS\", \"Per-test\", \"68.3\", \"2.1\", \"4x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B FT\", \"Per-test CLS\", \"75.5\", \"0.0\", \"0.5x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier: accuracy vs inference cost，标注所有model configurations\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B dominates 32B zero-shot on both accuracy AND cost——\n      这是论文efficiency narrative的强支持。Pareto frontier清晰展示fine-tuned classification\n      是当前最优cost-accuracy tradeoff。但需注意zero-shot baselines没有经过prompt engineering\n      优化，sophisticated prompting可能缩小gap。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: \"K=3 majority voting for per-test classification\"\n    expected_results:\n      single_pass_f1: 87.0\n      majority_k3_pass_f1: 88.4\n      single_fail_f1: 87.8\n      majority_k3_fail_f1: 89.1\n      accuracy_gain_pp: 1.2\n      inference_cost_multiplier: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting (K=3)通过self-consistency提供小幅提升（~1.2pp）。\n      在function-level上，模型的prediction已经较confident（87%+ F1），\n      大部分predictions在3次run中一致——improvement来自边界case的tiebreaking。\n      1.2pp gain with 3x cost在Pareto frontier上可能不如直接用更大模型cost-effective。\n      这个实验主要是completeness——展示test-time compute scaling在per-test上可以工作但\n      边际收益递减快。对于median档论文可能放到appendix。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1: Majority Voting Results (Function-Level)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Acc\", \"Cost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single (K=1)\", \"87.0\", \"87.8\", \"87.4\", \"1x\"]\n          - [\"Majority (K=3)\", \"88.4\", \"89.1\", \"88.7\", \"3x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"accuracy vs K curve (K=1,3,5), diminishing returns可视化\"\n    analysis: >\n      Majority voting提供modest gains，不足以改变论文main narrative。\n      可作为appendix展示test-time compute scaling dim，或在Pareto frontier中\n      提供additional data point。不建议作为main contribution。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7e613193-8e9c-4068-baa4-713d93e186c0","total_cost_usd":0.3377839999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10554,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"output_tokens":10414,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10554,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10414,"cache_read_input_tokens":11701,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10554,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10554},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5506,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005611,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10414,"cacheReadInputTokens":11701,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10554,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.33217299999999994,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"808ea6e3-615c-4162-a5ab-58dd4d5934ec"}
